# Pick — project rules

## What this is

Pick is a free-to-play prediction game on Robinhood Chain that onboards everyday users
into holding real-world assets (RWA). Users log in with X (an embedded wallet is created
for them). Each day they call "up" or "down" on exactly 10 of the ~194 tokenized RWA
stocks; the slate is submitted for the NEXT trading day and locks at 22:00 UTC the
evening before. Correct calls earn points; a leaderboard ranks players and resets on a
season cadence (start at 3-day, later daily). Top 20 earn RWA rewards; winners choose
which stock to be paid in.

The destination is ownership, not play: the point of the game is that a user with no
crypto knowledge ends up self-custodying real tokenized shares.

A separate passive path: a fee-on-transfer token (3% buy / 3% sell) splits tax 40% to
holders as RWA dividends (passive, claim anytime), 40% to leaderboard winners, and 20%
to new users who complete learn-to-earn tasks ($10 to the first 50 new users per season,
once per account, must share completion on X). Rewards are claimed in the Rewards tab
after connecting a wallet (MetaMask, Rabby, Coinbase, WalletConnect/Reown); on claim the
user picks which RWA stock to receive, then gets a shareable card.

## Hard rules — never violate

- NO betting, staking, or wagering. The game is free to play.
- Resolve picks off the mid of Robinhood's `/rhj/prices` quote, snapshotted once a day
 at 22:00 UTC, compared against the previous trading day's snapshot. Never off a DEX
 pool or spot token price: pool liquidity can be moved by anyone.
- Chainlink is the integrity anchor, not the settlement source. Where a covered ticker's
 feed disagrees with the REST mid beyond tolerance, VOID it rather than score it.
- A REST price is the raw underlying share price. Never multiply it by the token
 multiplier. A Chainlink answer already includes the multiplier, so divide it back out
 before comparing the two. Getting this backwards silently corrupts every result.
- Void, never guess. A ticker is voided for the slate on a corporate action in the
 window, a trading halt, a failed cross-check, an untradeable spread, or a missing
 price. A dividend or split moves the raw price for non-market reasons and would
 otherwise pay out every "down" call on a company that did not fall.
- A player's slate needs 7 of 10 scoreable tickers. Below that the whole slate voids and
 the streak is preserved: they showed up, the prices did not.
- A slate locks at the same instant its reference price is read. If those ever drift
 apart, players can watch the market move and still get in.
- One X account per player, with a minimum account age.
- Exactly 10 picks per slate. Not 9, not 11.
- No emojis in the UI or in code output. Use SVG line icons.
- Never say "gas", "seed phrase", "sign transaction" or "private key" in user-facing
 copy. The wallet is invisible; say "your wallet is set up for you".
- Gas sponsorship is testnet-only and pinned to the claim contract. Never widen
 `/api/aa/rpc` to sponsor an arbitrary target: a paymaster open to any call is a
 paymaster balance someone else spends.
- Adoption numbers are evidence, not marketing. Holdings are read from the chain, never
 inferred from our own claim rows, and retention counts only cohorts old enough to have
 had the chance.

## Stack

Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind. Privy for auth and embedded wallets.
wagmi + viem + Reown AppKit for external wallets. Supabase for Postgres, RLS, and cron.
Foundry for contracts. Deployed on Vercel.

## Chain

Contracts deploy to Robinhood Chain testnet: chainId 46630, RPC
https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com, explorer
https://explorer.testnet.chain.robinhood.com. Testnet stock tokens available from the
faucet: TSLA, AMZN, PLTR, NFLX, AMD.

Prices are read from mainnet: chainId 4663, RPC https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
(prefer `ALCHEMY_RPC_URL`), explorer https://robinhoodchain.blockscout.com. The real
Stock Tokens and their Chainlink feeds exist only there, so the game reads mainnet
prices while claims settle in testnet mocks until the contracts are audited.

## Data-source policy

All integrations and data use Robinhood Chain ecosystem partners — Robinhood `/rhj` REST
(`/assets`, `/prices`, `/corporate-actions`), Chainlink, Alchemy (RPC + Data/Prices +
account abstraction), Uniswap, Morpho, Paxos/USDG, Zerion — with EXACTLY ONE documented
exception: a single news provider (`NEWS_API_KEY`, Finnhub) used only for stock-detail
news, isolated in `src/lib/server/news.ts`, because no partner supplies equity news. Do
not add any other non-partner data source (no Polygon.io, no Twelve Data).

Concretely:

- Universe and token addresses: `/rhj/assets`. Never hardcode an address — a token with
 a matching ticker at another address is not a Robinhood Stock Token.
- Prices and resolution: `/rhj/prices`, cross-checked against Chainlink.
- Corporate actions: `/rhj/corporate-actions`.
- Charts: our own `price_snapshots` table, enriched by Alchemy's Prices API.
- Balances, RPC, gas sponsorship: Alchemy (Zerion may enrich balances).
- News: `news.ts` only. It must stay the single non-partner network call in the app.

## Design language

- Premium white. Background near-white with a faint green radial glow.
- Cards: white, hairline border `rgba(11,15,12,0.09)`, radius 16-20px, soft shadows.
- Font Manrope 400-800 via `next/font`.
- Ink `#0B0F0C`, muted `#5C665F`, faint `#8A938C`, wash `#F4F7F5`.
- Green `#00C805`, deep green `#068A3A` for green text on white, red `#FF5A52` for
  "down" and losses.
- Tabular figures on every number: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.
- Mobile-first. Full-bleed on phones, centered ~430px frame on desktop.
- Respect safe-area insets and `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- `tell-preview.html` (in the repo root) is the visual source of truth. It is branded
  "Tell", an older working name — the app is called Pick.

## Code conventions

- Tailwind for layout and one-off styles; design tokens live as CSS variables in
  `src/app/globals.css` and are mirrored into `tailwind.config.ts`.
- Server-only secrets (`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `PRIVY_APP_SECRET`,
  `CLAIM_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY`, `ALCHEMY_API_KEY`, `ALCHEMY_TESTNET_RPC_URL`,
  `ALCHEMY_GAS_POLICY_ID`, `ADMIN_API_TOKEN`, `NEWS_API_KEY`) must never be imported into
  a client component.
- Validate every API route body with zod.
- Prefer server-side data access through `src/lib/db` (service role) over direct
  browser-to-Supabase writes, because auth is Privy rather than Supabase Auth.
- The app must keep running when env vars are missing: fall back to demo data and say
  so in the UI.

## Before mainnet

Professional audit of all contracts, real DEX liquidity with oracle-based slippage
guards, legal review of the reward mechanics, and real terms/privacy pages.
